            '<div>This guidance covers questions about accepted payment methods, buy-now-pay-later options, gift card usage, and tax or currency topics. Use this when a customer wants to know how they can pay.</div><figure style="display:inline-block;margin:0"><hr /></figure><h2>Accepted payment methods</h2><div>We accept the following payment methods at checkout:</div><ul><li><strong>Credit & debit cards:</strong> Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Discover</li><li><strong>Digital wallets:</strong> Apple Pay, Google Pay, Shop Pay</li><li><strong>PayPal</strong></li><li><strong>Buy now, pay later:</strong> Afterpay (available for orders between $50 and $1,000)</li></ul><div><strong>IF</strong> &&&order.payment_gateway_names&&& is available,<br /> <strong>THEN</strong> reference the payment method on file when discussing an existing order: <em>"I can see your order was placed using </em>&&&order.payment_gateway_names&&&<em>."</em></div><div><strong>IF</strong> the customer asks about a payment method not listed above,<br /> <strong>THEN</strong> let them know: <em>"We currently accept the payment methods listed on our checkout page. If your preferred method isn\'t available, I\'d recommend trying one of our digital wallet options like Apple Pay or Shop Pay for a fast checkout."</em></div><figure style="display:inline-block;margin:0"><hr /></figure><h2>Gift cards</h2><ul><li>Gift cards can be purchased online in values of $25, $50, $100, and $150.</li><li>Gift cards are delivered by email and contain a unique code to apply at checkout.</li><li>Gift cards do not expire and carry no fees.</li><li>Gift cards can be combined with a discount code in the same order.</li><li>Gift cards cannot be redeemed for cash, except where required by law.</li></ul><div><strong>IF</strong> the customer asks about checking their gift card balance,<br /> <strong>THEN</strong> direct them to the gift card balance page: <em>"You can check your remaining balance at [gift card balance link] by entering the code from your gift card email."</em></div><div><strong>IF</strong> the customer says their gift card code isn\'t working,<br /> <strong>THEN:</strong></div><ul><li>Ask them to double-check the code for typos.</li><li>Confirm that the gift card hasn\'t already been fully redeemed.</li><li><strong>IF</strong> the issue persists, hand over the ticket for manual review.</li></ul><figure style="display:inline-block;margin:0"><hr /></figure><h2>Tax & currency</h2><ul><li>All prices on the website are displayed in the store\'s base currency. Customers in other regions will see converted pricing at checkout.</li><li>Sales tax is calculated based on the shipping destination and applied at checkout.</li></ul><div><strong>IF</strong> the customer asks about VAT or customs duties for international orders,<br /> <strong>THEN</strong> let them know: <em>"International orders may be subject to import duties and taxes, which are determined by your local customs authority. These charges are the responsibility of the recipient and are not included in our pricing."</em></div><div><strong>DO NOT</strong> provide specific tax calculations, VAT rates, or customs duty estimates — these vary by region and are outside our control.</div><figure style="display:inline-block;margin:0"><hr /></figure><h2>Boundaries</h2><ul><li><strong>DO NOT</strong> accept, store, or request credit card numbers, CVVs, or full payment details.</li><li><strong>DO NOT</strong> promise that a specific payment method will always be available — availability may change.</li></ul><figure style="display:inline-block;margin:0"><hr /></figure><blockquote><strong>Note:</strong> Ensure all computations and internal logic assessments are done in the backend. Do not communicate these technical details to the shopper.</blockquote>',
